{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://sugarcubes.dev/contracts/desktop-session/v1",
  "title": "Desktop session v1",
  "description": "Closed semantic snapshot and bounded chunk-transfer protocol. The installation namespace reuses the installed record owner's canonical 32-character lowercase hexadecimal InstallationId. The profile namespace reuses configuration ProfileId: 1..64 ASCII letters, digits, underscore or hyphen, preserving case (including real). Other durable identities are canonical lowercase non-nil UUIDs. Revisions are nonnegative JavaScript-safe integers; equality fences include webview and every fresh runtime binding. capturedAt is Unix milliseconds. Output list/batch/image and scene order coordinates are zero-based. Scene null denotes an ordinary submission without a scene group. Bounds and workArea are logical desktop pixels at captured dpi. Inspection matches CanvasInspection: mode fit/native/custom, image-relative centers, and normalized image distance per physical display pixel in spanX/spanY. Shared linked inspection is separate from retained per-output individual inspection; final outputs only. Paths name backend-relative descriptors, never native authority. graphJson is an encoded JSON object interpreted by Comfy. Session directories are sessions/<configured profile>/ below InstallationLayout::user(); originals, previous checkpoint and referenced assets are must-preserve. Unknown versions/fields fail closed and original bytes must be retained by the store. Import existing WorkflowViews.v1 only when no native checkpoint exists; retain browser records until durable acknowledgment. Transfer begin declares exact UTF-8 byte count, SHA-256 and chunk count; ordered chunks are at Unicode boundaries and at most 65536 UTF-8 bytes; commit requires all chunks and digest verification. Only the publishing host emits durable acknowledgment. Optional capabilities require unsupported when absent. Origin must equal the independently authorized current frontend origin; no wire field grants privilege. Capture/materialize require committed workflow lifecycle and current complete fences. Live execution/restore policy and transport lifecycle belong to their application owners. Entries are ordered document occurrences: rename/Save As keeps the entry ID; duplicate allocates a fresh ID even for identical graphs. Accepted submissions persist prompt/backend/run/source/scene identity before outputs exist. Outputs with promptId must match the accepted submission and its frozen source snapshot. Restore creates explicit snapshot provenance and never replays generation events. Existing WorkflowViews.v1 imports may lack editorWidth; its owner supplies the current default. Session asset filenames derive from digest plus validated extension and remain below user/sessions/<profile>/assets. Transfer indexes are zero-based and every request has one observed terminal outcome; cancellation does not prove native work stopped. Navigation persists scene All independently of batch-grid and artifact inspection: sceneOverview=true requires sceneId=null; otherwise null sceneId denotes ordinary submissions. batchOverview denotes the batch grid; batchIndex retains its last position while the grid is active. Source and explicit scene/batch positions must belong to the same entry, including its accepted pending submissions. The session backend UUID is a durable namespace correlation key, not BackendTarget, ResourceKey or BackendCustodyKey. The host must bind it to its existing admitted BackendTarget and freshly verified current custody, never adopt a checkpoint backend value as authority. Ready carries complete current bindings and is republished at committed semantic changes. Scope/origin/fresh webview identity are supplied by the trusted host bootstrap before occurrence proposals. The host owns occurrence adoption. Fence.revision is a frontend observation revision within that webview; equal revisions require identical bindings, older/wrong-webview announcements are stale. Capture.revision is a distinct host-assigned durable checkpoint revision, shared by checkpoint, transfer and acknowledgement; it never resets with frontend observation revision. baselineGraphJson preserves the Comfy change-tracker initial graph; null means initial state was unavailable. Current plus baseline graphs must fit one 33554432-byte UTF-8 document budget before graph decoding, and the encoded document envelope shares that same budget. No transfer limit is increased. Placement bounds are normal OUTER window bounds even while maximized/minimized. bounds and workArea positions/extents are physical SCREEN coordinates divided uniformly by captured reference-monitor scale dpi/96. Restore uses logical offset bounds.xy-workArea.xy, then target physical position=target workArea physical origin+offset*target scale and outer size=bounds.size*target scale, followed by native clamping/minimum-size validation before reveal. monitor is the nonempty native device name without control characters (including NUL); it grants no native authority. Host bootstrap uses observation revision 0 and no bindings; the first frontend Ready observation has a positive revision (start 1). At the same observation revision, bindings, committed state, persistence choice and advertised capabilities are immutable; semantic changes advance that revision.",
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/SessionCheckpoint"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/SessionMessage"
    }
  ],
